Same-router fallback addresses (patches/net-0006), as melee-unlocked does them (its port/runtime/hle/slippi_address.h and the
public_fallbacks of its NetplayClient): when the matchmaking ticket gives the other player the same public address as this
one, the LAN address is dialled first (as before) and, if it has not answered in 2 s, the public address too, within the same
8 s budget; the other side's connection from its public address is accepted. Two players behind one router (or a guest
network, or two routers behind one public address) connect where the LAN address alone could not. Slippi Dolphin 3.7.0 dials
only the LAN address in that case; nothing on the wire changes.
Applied by ../net_sources.sh after net-0005. port/ is unchanged.

